        "acceptedPr": null,
        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Markdown fence detection rewritten as stateful line parser",
        "summary": "The streaming markdown renderer in the CLI now tracks open code fences with a line-based state machine instead of counting backtick triplets. A new `LOOSE_FENCE_LINE` regex and `nextOpenFence` helper determine whether a fence is open, closed, or nonexistent, correctly handling indented lists, blockquotes, and the CommonMark rule that backtick runs with backticks in their info string do not open fences. `renderStreamingMarkdown` and `renderStreamingMarkdownIncremental` now call `openBacktickFenceIndex` to locate the pending fence, replacing previous `lastIndexOf` and even/odd count logic that misidentified mid-sentence ` ``` ` as fence boundaries.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff replaces the naive `hasIncompleteCodeFence` implementation (which counted ` ``` ` occurrences modulo 2) with a line-by-line state machine using the new `LOOSE_FENCE_LINE` regex and `nextOpenFence` helper, and updates `renderStreamingMarkdown` and `renderStreamingMarkdownIncremental` to use `openBacktickFenceIndex` instead of `lastIndexOf`. New tests assert that fences nested in lists or blockquotes are correctly tracked and that backtick runs with info-string backticks do not open fences.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "whyMissing": true,
